From acd4b7f9edd039f2808e4b3473d9082985de02f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local-crawl <local-crawl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:48:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Scrape fixes: full CSS selectors in includeTags, clear
 no-match, no leaked page machinery

includeTags / excludeTags
- Run every selector on the whole rendered document before the boilerplate
  cleanup (Firecrawl's order). Before, the cleanup ran first, so a selector
  reaching into a <header>, an <aside> or a `.promo` card matched nothing.
  The cleanup still runs inside a selection but never removes a selected
  element.
- excludeTags detaches matches from the parsed tree and re-serializes with
  html5ever, so descendant selectors work across the selection and text is
  escaped correctly. Nested include matches are emitted once, in document
  order.
- A successful includeTags narrowing is final, like css/xpath: no readability
  re-narrowing, no alternates ladder, no title/description padding. Before, a
  short selection (a list of prices) scored as low quality and was replaced by
  the captured-XHR candidate, i.e. a consent banner's CSS and tokens.
- Warnings: invalid selectors (`invalid_selector: ...`), selectors that
  matched nothing beside ones that did (`include_tags_partial_match: ...`),
  and a readable `include_tags_no_match: includeTags matched 0 elements (...)`
  next to `selector_no_match`. metadata.includeTagsMatches carries per-selector
  counts.

Page machinery
- Strip <template> along with script/style/noscript.
- Never fall back to the raw HTML when cleaning fails; fall back to the
  document with non-content tags removed.
- The XHR text candidate only keeps strings that read as prose (no markup,
  CSS rules, JWTs, base64 or code-like punctuation).
- onlyMainContent also removes consent managers whose containers say neither
  "cookie" nor "consent": Osano, Quantcast Choice, Didomi, Usercentrics,
  Sourcepoint, iubenda.

Rendering
- A blank ws_url switches a CDP tier off. Before, `[renderer.lightpanda]
  ws_url = ""` kept LightPanda in the ladder and every JS render failed on it
  first (reported as lightpandaCrash).
- A 2xx page with fewer than 20 characters of text gets one try on the next
  tier of the auto ladder, then an `empty_content: ...` warning listing the
  renderers tried.

PDF
- pdf_not_a_pdf / corrupt warnings include the HTTP status, declared
  Content-Type, size and the HTML <title> or first ~200 characters.
